1
00:02:18,563 --> 00:02:20,110
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۞

2
00:02:20,200 --> 00:02:21,592
بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۞

3
00:02:22,976 --> 00:02:27,057
رَبِّ اشْرَحْ لِي صَدْرِي۞ وَيَسِّرْ لِي أَمْرِي۞وَاحْلُلْ عُقْدَةً مِنْ لِسَانِيْ۞ يَفْقَهُوا قَوْلِيِ۞

4
00:02:27,973 --> 00:02:33,600
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمدوَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا

5
00:02:35,521 --> 00:02:39,446
We ask Allahسبحانه وتعالى to bless this gathering.

6
00:02:39,693 --> 00:02:43,290
We ask Allahسبحانه وتعالى to benefit us, from what we learn.

7
00:02:43,961 --> 00:02:48,312
We ask Allahسبحانه وتعالى to teach us that, which will benefit us.

8
00:02:49,182 --> 00:02:54,130
We ask Allahسبحانه وتعالى to make us of those, who will follow the way of Rasool Allah ﷺ and love him.

9
00:02:55,062 --> 00:02:58,614
And we ask Allahسبحانه وتعالى to make us of those, who will be with him in Jannah(جنة).

10
00:03:00,878 --> 00:03:05,218
First of all, we'll start with definition of Seerah(سيرة).

11
00:03:05,305 --> 00:03:07,149
What does the word Seerah(سيرة) mean?

12
00:03:09,136 --> 00:03:13,606
The word, Seerah(سيرة) has a linguistic meaning and that is a path,

13
00:03:15,172 --> 00:03:17,592
and walking is called Sair(سير).

14
00:03:18,173 --> 00:03:21,135
When you walk from one place to another, it says, Saraa Fulaan(سَارَ فُلَانْ).

15
00:03:21,922 --> 00:03:24,616
Fulaan(فلان) is walking, or such as this person is walking.

16
00:03:25,625 --> 00:03:31,810
So, it is the path that a person takes, during their lifetime, that is Seerah(سيرة).

17
00:03:32,699 --> 00:03:39,348
And the Hans Wehr dictionary, gives the translation of the word Seerah(سيرة) as

18
00:03:39,677 --> 00:03:50,226
conduct, comportment, demeanor, behavior, way of life, attitude, position, reaction, way of acting and biography.

19
00:03:50,282 --> 00:03:52,173
All of these are meanings of the word Seerah(سيرة).

20
00:03:53,982 --> 00:03:58,494
And Seerah(سيرة) could be the biography of any person, it not necessarily Muhammadﷺ.

21
00:03:58,558 --> 00:04:04,322
However, we have used the word so much with Muhammadﷺ, that when we say Seerah(سيرة),

22
00:04:05,580 --> 00:04:10,112
we almost, all the time, are referring to, The Life of Muhammadﷺ.

23
00:04:11,055 --> 00:04:15,089
But you could also say the Seerah(سيرة) of Abu Bakr(ابو بكر), the Seerah(سيرة) of Umar(عمر), the Seerah(سيرة) of so and so.

24
00:04:15,485 --> 00:04:17,966
It is a biography of a person, their life.

25
00:04:18,418 --> 00:04:22,191
So, that's the meaning of the word Seerah(سيرة), it is the life of a person,

26
00:04:22,373 --> 00:04:26,794
and in this situation, we're studying the life of the greatest; Muhammadﷺ.

27
00:04:28,076 --> 00:04:30,755
What's the importance of studying Seerah(سيرة)?

28
00:04:31,682 --> 00:04:32,861
Number one;

29
00:04:33,395 --> 00:04:37,481
The life of Muhammadﷺ is the history of Islam;

30
00:04:38,482 --> 00:04:43,713
you're studying a Concise History of Islam by studying, The Life Of Muhammadﷺ.

31
00:04:45,144 --> 00:04:54,837
His life; in His Seerah(سيرة), we would find situations and incidences that would help us

32
00:04:55,332 --> 00:04:59,945
in everything that we would need to know, in our life of Da'wah(دعوة).

33
00:05:01,267 --> 00:05:04,326
So, the life of Muhammadﷺ is really the history of Islam.

34
00:05:05,727 --> 00:05:09,865
We're not just studying the biography of a person, we're studying history of our religion.

35
00:05:12,040 --> 00:05:14,179
Muhammad Ibn Sa'ad Bin Abi Waqas(محمد ابن سعد بن ابي وقاص),

36
00:05:15,027 --> 00:05:17,455
- Sa'ad Ibn Abi Waqas(سعد إبن وقاص) is one of Ashra Mubashireen Bil Jannah(عشره مبشرين بالجنة),

37
00:05:17,687 --> 00:05:20,283
he is one of the ten(10), who were given glad tidings of paradise.

38
00:05:20,798 --> 00:05:22,637
His son Muhammad(محمد) says:

39
00:05:23,482 --> 00:05:28,086
That our father would teach us the battles of Rasool Allahﷺ,

40
00:05:28,126 --> 00:05:30,483
he would teach us the Seerah(سيرة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ

41
00:05:31,349 --> 00:05:35,629
and he would tell us that these are the traditions of your fathers.

42
00:05:35,906 --> 00:05:36,830
So, study them.!

43
00:05:38,141 --> 00:05:40,590
And they used to refer to Seerah(سيرة), as Maghazi(مغازي),

44
00:05:41,372 --> 00:05:42,860
Maghazi(مغازي) means the battles,

45
00:05:43,258 --> 00:05:46,817
because the latter part of Rasool Allah ﷺ was spent in Maghazi(مغازي).

46
00:05:47,280 --> 00:05:51,786
So, they would use this word Maghazi(مغازي) to refer to, The Whole life of Muhammadﷺ.

47
00:05:52,363 --> 00:05:54,505
And Ali Bin Hussain Ibn Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي بن حسين ابن علي ابن ابي طالب),

48
00:05:54,545 --> 00:05:57,482
the grandson of Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب), he would say that,

49
00:05:57,853 --> 00:06:01,523
we were taught the Seerah(سيرة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ, like we were taught Qur'an.

50
00:06:02,430 --> 00:06:04,543
That is how important Seerah(سيرة) was for them.

51
00:06:04,972 --> 00:06:07,154
They would study it, like they would study Qur'an.

52
00:06:08,059 --> 00:06:14,494
And that makes sense, because if you want to study the life of Musaعليه السلام, where do we go.?

53
00:06:15,327 --> 00:06:16,738
where do we study it from?

54
00:06:17,336 --> 00:06:18,844
From Qur'an.

55
00:06:19,074 --> 00:06:22,624
If we want to study the life of Eesaعليه السلام,

56
00:06:23,224 --> 00:06:25,163
we go to Qur'an.

57
00:06:25,712 --> 00:06:28,729
But if we want to study the life of Muhammadﷺ,

58
00:06:29,812 --> 00:06:35,180
His life, even though there are bits and pieces of it, mentioned in Qur'an,

59
00:06:35,742 --> 00:06:41,413
but we don't have as much details about the life of Muhammadﷺ in Qur'an, as we have about Musa(موسى).

60
00:06:42,575 --> 00:06:46,475
So, the life of Rasool Allah ﷺ for us, to study it, we go to Seerah(سيرة).

61
00:06:47,627 --> 00:06:51,866
All of the Ambiyaa(أنبياء), their lives were recorded in Qur'an, with the exception of Muhammadﷺ,

62
00:06:52,232 --> 00:06:54,528
Muhammadﷺ, his life, we'd learn it from Seerah(سيرة).

63
00:06:55,289 --> 00:06:57,794
So, when we want to learn about the Ambiyaa(أنبياء), we go to Qur'an.

64
00:06:57,834 --> 00:07:01,256
When we want to learn about Muhammadﷺ we go to his Seerah(سيرة).

65
00:07:02,002 --> 00:07:05,586
Again - even though there's some references in Qur'an made to his life.

66
00:07:05,790 --> 00:07:08,803
We'll talk about the influence of Seerah(سيرة), in understanding Quran.

67
00:07:10,113 --> 00:07:10,909
Number two!

68
00:07:11,062 --> 00:07:14,485
The second reason for studying Seerah(سيرة).

69
00:07:15,093 --> 00:07:19,284
It is to develop the proper love of Muhammadﷺ, in our hearts.

70
00:07:20,267 --> 00:07:22,503
Loving Muhammadﷺ is Ibadah(عبادة)

71
00:07:22,964 --> 00:07:26,313
It's part of our religion to love Muhammad صلوات الله وسلام عليه,

72
00:07:26,384 --> 00:07:27,023
He says:

73
00:07:27,773 --> 00:07:32,843
لَا يُؤمِنُ أحَدَكُمْ حَتَّى أَكُوْنَ أَحَبَّ إِلَيْهِ مِنْ وَلِدَهِ وَوَالَدِهِ وَالنَّاسِ أَجْمَعِيْنْ۞

74
00:07:34,027 --> 00:07:36,291
One of you does not attain true faith,

75
00:07:36,757 --> 00:07:40,512
until you love me more than you love your parents, your children and the whole world.

76
00:07:42,180 --> 00:07:47,417
We don't really become true believers, until we love Muhammadﷺ more than anything else.

77
00:07:48,172 --> 00:07:51,771
So, it is part of Islam, to love Muhammadﷺ.

78
00:07:53,533 --> 00:07:56,967
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه, he came to Muhammadﷺ and said:

79
00:07:58,040 --> 00:08:01,735
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was very honest and straightforward person,

80
00:08:01,793 --> 00:08:07,124
he went to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said, O Rasool Ullah, I love you more than everything except myself.

81
00:08:08,402 --> 00:08:11,603
I love you more than anyone, except myself.

82
00:08:12,368 --> 00:08:16,036
Rasool Allah ﷺ, told him:

83
00:08:16,677 --> 00:08:18,042
 Until you love me.

84
00:08:19,321 --> 00:08:26,410
Meaning, you don't really attain the complete faith, until you love me more than your own self.

85
00:08:26,866 --> 00:08:32,176
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) came back and said: O Rasool Ullah, now I love you more than my own self.

86
00:08:32,651 --> 00:08:33,764
Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

87
00:08:33,865 --> 00:08:34,430
اَلْآنَ اِذَنْ

88
00:08:34,470 --> 00:08:37,871
Now, you have attained the complete faith.

89
00:08:40,176 --> 00:08:43,598
The Ummah(امة) today, loves Muhammadﷺ.

90
00:08:44,352 --> 00:08:47,679
If you ask any Muslim, do you love Muhammadﷺ? They would say: Yes!

91
00:08:48,804 --> 00:08:54,897
But the love cannot be very deep and sincere, unless you know the person.

92
00:08:56,043 --> 00:08:59,879
If you have shallow information about someone, you can't really love them a lot.

93
00:09:00,772 --> 00:09:02,765
To love a person, you need to know them more.

94
00:09:03,265 --> 00:09:06,779
And this is especially true with Muhammadﷺ because the more you know him,

95
00:09:07,146 --> 00:09:10,238
the more you would be impressed with his personality, the more you would love him.

96
00:09:11,812 --> 00:09:20,237
So, even though Muhammadﷺ among the Ummah(امة) today with the shallow information that the masses of the Muslims have, about him,

97
00:09:20,714 --> 00:09:22,175
even though they still love him,

98
00:09:22,786 --> 00:09:29,048
but we cannot truly have deep love to Muhammadﷺ unless we know him.

99
00:09:30,072 --> 00:09:34,681
You know, the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم the more they knew him,

100
00:09:34,718 --> 00:09:36,576
the closer they were to him, the more they would love him.

101
00:09:36,616 --> 00:09:37,695
Amr Bin Aas(عمرو بن العاص) for example,

102
00:09:38,362 --> 00:09:42,357
he was one of the staunchest enemies of Muhammad صلوات الله وسلام عليه.

103
00:09:43,467 --> 00:09:47,032
He was one of the top plotters against Islam.

104
00:09:48,214 --> 00:09:52,766
Amr Bin Aas(عمرو بن العاص), he later became a Muslim and when he was passing away,

105
00:09:53,974 --> 00:09:56,980
Amr Bin Aas(عمرو بن العاص) started weeping, he was crying, on his death bed.

106
00:09:58,072 --> 00:10:00,818
So, his son Abdullah Bin Amr(عبدالله بن عمرو) told him:

107
00:10:00,867 --> 00:10:04,627
O my father, didn't Rasool Allah ﷺ give you the glad tidings of this,

108
00:10:04,738 --> 00:10:06,619
didn't he give you the glad tidings of that.

109
00:10:06,942 --> 00:10:09,333
I mean, it is reported in Hadith, that Rasool Allahﷺ said:

110
00:10:09,428 --> 00:10:10,251
آمَنَ عمرو

111
00:10:10,809 --> 00:10:14,098
That Amr Bin Aas(عمرو بن العاص) has attained faith.

112
00:10:14,646 --> 00:10:17,598
So, this is a witness from Rasool Allahﷺ, that Amr Bin Aas(عمرو بن العاص) is a Mo'min(مؤمن),

113
00:10:17,915 --> 00:10:20,732
 not only a Muslim, but he is the higher level of Mo'min(مؤمن).

114
00:10:22,535 --> 00:10:26,996
So, his son was trying to give his father the glad tidings that you are a true believer.

115
00:10:27,138 --> 00:10:30,694
 I mean, Rasool Allahﷺ has given you all of these, glad tidings.

116
00:10:30,757 --> 00:10:33,688
 How come you are crying now before, your death.

117
00:10:34,292 --> 00:10:37,542
Amr Bin Aas(عمرو بن العاص), he turned around, and he said,

118
00:10:38,562 --> 00:10:41,203
I have went through three stages in my life.

119
00:10:42,052 --> 00:10:43,350
At the first stage,

120
00:10:44,153 --> 00:10:48,015
the most despised man to me, was Muhammadﷺ.

121
00:10:48,952 --> 00:10:52,199
And my desire was that I could get my hold of him,

122
00:10:52,702 --> 00:10:54,621
I could get my hands on him and kill him.

123
00:10:55,282 --> 00:11:00,941
That was my desire, that was my wish, my aspiration to kill Muhammadﷺ.

124
00:11:01,562 --> 00:11:05,174
He says; If I died at that time, I would have definitely been in Hellfire.

125
00:11:06,032 --> 00:11:08,750
He said than Allah put the love of Islam in my heart.

126
00:11:09,819 --> 00:11:13,192
And I went to Muhammadﷺ and I said, O Muhammad(محمد).

127
00:11:13,922 --> 00:11:15,223
I want to become Muslim,

128
00:11:15,832 --> 00:11:19,344
extend your hand, so that I can pledge allegiance to you,

129
00:11:20,362 --> 00:11:24,836
Amr Bin Aas(عمرو بن العاص) says; Muhammadﷺ extended his hand forward,

130
00:11:25,982 --> 00:11:27,515
and I pulled my hand away.

131
00:11:28,252 --> 00:11:31,351
So, Amr Bin Aas(عمرو بن العاص), he had Rasool Allahﷺ extend his hand,

132
00:11:31,632 --> 00:11:34,862
and when Rasool Allahﷺ was ready to put his hand, in his.

133
00:11:35,022 --> 00:11:36,706
Amr Bin Aas(عمرو بن العاص), Pulled his hand away.

134
00:11:36,972 --> 00:11:38,782
Rasool Allahﷺ told him: What's wrong.?

135
00:11:39,392 --> 00:11:41,462
Amr Bin Aas(عمرو بن العاص) said: I have a condition to make.

136
00:11:42,102 --> 00:11:43,516
اُرِيْدُ اَنْ تَشْتَرِطُ لِنَفْسِيْ

137
00:11:43,846 --> 00:11:45,931
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him: What is your condition.?

138
00:11:46,482 --> 00:11:50,023
He said: My condition is that, you pardon me.

139
00:11:51,292 --> 00:11:52,052
You give me clemency

140
00:11:52,092 --> 00:11:55,835
because Amr Bin Aas(عمرو بن العاص) knew that what he has done in the past,

141
00:11:57,211 --> 00:12:04,056
the great crimes that he committed against the Muslims, is sufficient for his execution.

142
00:12:04,652 --> 00:12:09,356
So, he wanted to make sure that Rasool Allah ﷺ would not hold him accountable for what he did in the past,

143
00:12:10,122 --> 00:12:11,826
Rasool Allah ﷺ smiled and he said:

144
00:12:11,888 --> 00:12:15,497
يَا عمرو: اَمَا تَدْرِي اَنَّ لْاِسْلَامَ يَجُبُّ مَا قَبْلَهَ،

145
00:12:16,417 --> 00:12:18,621
وَاَنَّ الْهِجْرَتَ تَجُبُّ مَا قَبْلَهَا،

146
00:12:19,941 --> 00:12:21,943
وَ اَنَّ الْحَجَّ يَجُبُّ مَا قَبْلَهَ

147
00:12:22,652 --> 00:12:27,954
"O Amr(عمرو): Don't you know, that Islam erases everything before it,

148
00:12:28,812 --> 00:12:31,267
and Hijrah(هجرة) erases everything before it,

149
00:12:32,052 --> 00:12:34,842
and Hajj(حج), erases everything before it."

150
00:12:36,272 --> 00:12:38,499
Amr Bin Aas(عمرو بن العاص) said: So, I became Muslim.

151
00:12:39,192 --> 00:12:40,762
He said at that stage,

152
00:12:41,691 --> 00:12:47,521
Muhammadﷺ, who was my worst enemy, became the most beloved person to me in the world.

153
00:12:48,402 --> 00:12:50,387
He said: And I loved him so much,

154
00:12:50,919 --> 00:12:52,673
and I respected him so much,

155
00:12:53,142 --> 00:12:56,419
I couldn't even get a full glimpse of his face.

156
00:12:56,776 --> 00:12:59,855
Whenever, I would see him, I would stare downwards.

157
00:12:59,895 --> 00:13:05,802
He said: I have so much love, and respect for him, I couldn't even get a full glimpse of his face,

158
00:13:06,092 --> 00:13:09,573
and if you would ask me today, to describe him to you, I couldn't.

159
00:13:10,724 --> 00:13:13,850
He said: and if I died during that stage.

160
00:13:14,740 --> 00:13:17,432
I would have hoped to be in Jannah(جنة).

161
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:21,718
And then he said, and then later on, came things and we don't know, where we stand?

162
00:13:22,182 --> 00:13:25,567
Anyway, there's some other parts for the Hadith(حديث)

163
00:13:25,962 --> 00:13:29,322
but the part that concerns us now is that Amr Bin Aas(عمرو بن العاص)

164
00:13:29,422 --> 00:13:33,406
when he got to know Muhammadﷺ, when he became close to him.

165
00:13:34,440 --> 00:13:39,130
Muhammadﷺ, who was his worst enemy became his most beloved friend.

166
00:13:41,137 --> 00:13:43,981
Sohail Bin Amr(سهيل بن عمرو), was sent by Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

167
00:13:44,552 --> 00:13:47,495
to negotiate with Muhammadﷺ before Sulh-Hal-Hudaubiyah(صلح الحديبيه)

168
00:13:48,662 --> 00:13:51,924
Sohail Bin Amr(سهيل بن عمرو) was, an international negotiator,

169
00:13:51,979 --> 00:13:58,693
he has been to the courts of the Persian Emperor, the Roman Emperor, the Emperor of Abyssinia.

170
00:13:59,424 --> 00:14:00,990
He's a well connected man.

171
00:14:01,692 --> 00:14:07,129
And now, Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) sent him to negotiate with Muhammadﷺ.

172
00:14:07,200 --> 00:14:10,451
So he went into Madina and he came in

173
00:14:11,332 --> 00:14:18,135
and he had firsthand experience with, how the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم treat Muhammadﷺ.

174
00:14:19,073 --> 00:14:23,523
So, Sohail Bin Amr(سهيل بن عمرو) went back to report, to Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) He told them,

175
00:14:24,203 --> 00:14:29,210
He said: I've visited the Roman Emperor,

176
00:14:30,011 --> 00:14:31,766
I've visited the Persian Emperor,

177
00:14:32,344 --> 00:14:34,490
I've visited An-Najashi(نجاشي) of Abyssinia,

178
00:14:35,542 --> 00:14:46,587
but I have never in my life, seen a leader that is so loved by his followers and so much respected by his followers, like Muhammadﷺ.

179
00:14:47,432 --> 00:14:49,389
I have seen nothing like it, in the world.

180
00:14:51,391 --> 00:14:54,523
The Roman Emperor, the Persian Emperor, An-Najashi(نجاشي) of Abyssinia,

181
00:14:55,088 --> 00:14:58,296
even though they have all of the power and strength and empires.

182
00:14:58,643 --> 00:15:04,146
I have never seen a people, love their leader so much like the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم loved Muhammadﷺ.

183
00:15:04,552 --> 00:15:06,194
He said: I saw amazing things.

184
00:15:06,413 --> 00:15:13,697
